cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Behavioral SETI — analysis code"
message: "If you use this software or its derived results, please cite the paper."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Griffin
    given-names: Robert
    affiliation: "Dxtra Inc."
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-13
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dxtrainc/behavioral-seti"
url: "https://dxtra.com/static/galactic-dx/index.html"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a combination-space search for embedded technosignatures in
  public solar and heliospheric archives. The carrier is taken to be a
  dimensionless relationship among observables rather than a named channel, so
  the search space can be enumerated and its coverage measured. Twenty-nine
  searches: twenty-five null, three void, one a known signal recovered as a
  positive control.
keywords:
  - SETI
  - behavioral SETI
  - technosignatures
  - Fermi paradox
  - zoo hypothesis
  - solar irradiance
  - heliophysics
  - helioseismology
  - time-series analysis
  - surrogate data
  - reproducible research
